## A range is ( from MARKER to ) or ( from MARKER to .. step ) where MARKER is
## one of .< .<= .> .>= - the comparison the loop it stands for will perform.
## '..' introduces the step only, so it is never a range marker on its own.

(1 .. 10);  ##ERROR: syntax error - prohibited range operator around '..'

---

## only one comparison marker per range

(1 .< 2 .< 3);  ##ERROR: syntax error - prohibited range operator around '.<'

---

## and only one step

(1 .< 2 .. 3 .. 4);  ##ERROR: syntax error - prohibited range operator around '..'

---

## a marker is allowed after the first item only

(.< 1 2);  ##ERROR: syntax error - prohibited range operator around '.<'

---

## the end of the range is missing

(1 .<);  ##ERROR: syntax error - no operand after range operator '.<'

---

## so is the step

(1 .< 2 ..);  ##ERROR: syntax error - no operand after range operator '..'

---

## a range holds nothing beyond its end, or beyond its step

(1 .< 2 3);  ##ERROR: syntax error - redundant operand '3'
